# Presentation analysis rules

- Never recompute or alter statistical results solely for presentation.
- Presentation code may select, rename, order, filter, reshape, or combine existing outputs.
- Every presentation figure must record its source table in manifests.
- Never represent an unmeasurable effect as zero (H2/H3 are categorical unmeasurable).
- H2/H3 Stage 11 primary results are unmeasurable, not null.
- |Cliff's δ| >= 0.11 is the prespecified effect-size gate, not a p-value threshold.
- Open markers indicate thin measurement; grey/× indicates unmeasurable.
- Exploratory EES, attention, richness and quality/reach analyses must be labeled EXPLORATORY.
- Component effects must not be described as confirmation of parent H1–H6.
- Export every final chart as PNG + SVG + PDF.
- Save underlying presentation data as CSV before plotting.
- Never hard-code raw RAX/RLR/EES feature names into audience-facing figures; use theme_dictionary.csv.
- Danger×protection interaction is non-significant — do not use as main-slide evidence.
